Post-vendoring correction — Remove-KioskRunTasks.ps1 and Detect-KioskRunTasks.ps1
  (2026-09-03, applied after this NOTICE's initial hashes were recorded).
  These are owner-authored scripts; this is a correctness fix applied by the
  repository during its own phase-155 code review, not an upstream change.
  The orphaned kiosk-profile block read the current kiosk account name from
  the registry with `-ErrorAction SilentlyContinue` and used it unguarded as
  the exclusion key for a loop that (in Remove-KioskRunTasks.ps1) permanently
  deletes non-loaded `kioskUser*` profiles, and (in Detect-KioskRunTasks.ps1)
  reports them as orphaned. If that registry read ever returns null or empty,
  the unguarded comparison excluded nothing, so the loop would treat every
  non-loaded `kioskUser*` profile — including the currently-assigned one, if
  momentarily unloaded — as an orphan. A `-match '^kioskUser\d+$'` guard,
  identical in form to the one this same script already applies to the
  OneDrive-payload cleanup six lines below, now wraps both loops; when the
  guard fails, the run is skipped and a `WARN:` line is recorded instead of
  defaulting to "treat as orphan." Applied identically to both committed
  copies of Remove-KioskRunTasks.ps1 (package-sources/kiosk-baseline/Files/
  and remediations/run-task-cleanup/, re-confirmed byte-identical by SHA256
  after the edit) and to the single copy of Detect-KioskRunTasks.ps1. The
  hashes above reflect the corrected bytes.

